</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Methodology</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formulate the problem of prompt optimization problem not as directly fine-tuning model parameters, but as a task that maximizes the inherent reasoning capability of LLMs by facilitating learning from reference examplars. Specifically, our framework <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contrastive Reasoning Prompt Optimization (CRPO)</span> first retrieves the top-<math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> relevant prompts from the <em id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HelpSteer2</em> training set, and then applies contrastive reasoning to construct optimized prompts. We design two complementary variants, illustrated in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II Dataset ‣ Better by Comparison: Retrieval-Augmented Contrastive Reasoning for Automatic Prompt Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Retrieval of Reference Prompts</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given an input query <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, CRPO retrieves a set of reference prompts <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> using a retriever:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(q)=\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\},\quad p_{i}\in\text{HelpSteer2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mtext>HelpSteer2</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(q)=\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\},\quad p_{i}\in\text{HelpSteer2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is annotated along five evaluation dimensions <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{\text{help},\text{corr},\text{coh},\text{comp},\text{verb}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>help</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>corr</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>coh</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>comp</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>verb</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{\text{help},\text{corr},\text{coh},\text{comp},\text{verb}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. To ensure sufficient coverage across all dimensions, we require <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math>, so that at least one candidate prompt is available per metric. These exemplars serve as contrasting cases that enable the LLM to perform explicit reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Variant 1: Tiered Contrastive Reasoning</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We partition <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> into three tiers according to overall quality scores.
Specifically, for each retrieved prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute its average score across all five evaluation dimensions:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Avg}(p_{i})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{M}|}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\text{Score}(p_{i},m)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Avg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Avg}(p_{i})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{M}|}\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}}\text{Score}(p_{i},m),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{\text{help},\text{corr},\text{coh},\text{comp},\text{verb}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>help</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>corr</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>coh</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>comp</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>verb</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{\text{help},\text{corr},\text{coh},\text{comp},\text{verb}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Prompts are then partitioned into high-quality (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{H}</annotation></semantics></math>), medium-quality (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>), and low-quality (<math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>) tiers based on quantile thresholds of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Avg}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Avg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Avg}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimized prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated via contrastive reasoning:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}=f_{\theta}\big(\text{Reflect}(P^{H},P^{M},P^{L})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Reflect</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=f_{\theta}\big(\text{Reflect}(P^{H},P^{M},P^{L})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the LLM and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Reflect}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Reflect</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Reflect}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> instructs the model to (i) avoid weaknesses in <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, (ii) adopt strengths from <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (iii) use <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> as a stabilizing anchor that reduces bias.
In particular, incorporating <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents overfitting to extreme cases, ensuring balanced refinement that maintains robustness while still progressing toward high-quality prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Variant 2: Multi-Metric Contrastive Reasoning</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each metric <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, we select the top prompt:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{m}=\arg\max_{p_{i}\in\mathcal{R}(q)}\text{Score}(p_{i},m)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{m}=\arg\max_{p_{i}\in\mathcal{R}(q)}\text{Score}(p_{i},m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The optimized prompt is then constructed as:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}=f_{\theta}\big(\text{Integrate}(P^{\text{help}},P^{\text{corr}},P^{\text{coh}},P^{\text{comp}},P^{\text{verb}})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Integrate</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>help</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>coh</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mtext>verb</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=f_{\theta}\big(\text{Integrate}(P^{\text{help}},P^{\text{corr}},P^{\text{coh}},P^{\text{comp}},P^{\text{verb}})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Integrate}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Integrate</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Integrate}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> encourages the LLM to combine complementary strengths across evaluation axes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">III-D</span> </span><span id="S3.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Evaluation Method</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Effectiveness is assessed by directly feeding the original prompt <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimized prompt <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> into the evaluation model <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> as a pair. The evaluation model then outputs comparative scores across the five annotated dimensions <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Score}(p,p^{*})=\big[s_{\text{help}},s_{\text{corr}},s_{\text{coh}},s_{\text{comp}},s_{\text{verb}}\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>help</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>coh</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>verb</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Score}(p,p^{*})=\big[s_{\text{help}},s_{\text{corr}},s_{\text{coh}},s_{\text{comp}},s_{\text{verb}}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{m}\in[0,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{m}\in[0,4]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure consistency, these raw scores are normalized to the <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range and aggregated as described in Section 4. Improvements are thus attributed to contrastive reasoning in CRPO, since the evaluation model judges <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> relative to <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> under identical conditions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <em id="alg1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Contrastive Reasoning Prompt Optimization (CRPO)</em></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            Query <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, Retriever <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, LLM <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, Evaluation Model <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, Metrics <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Top-<math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// Retrieval Stage</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
            Retrieve prompts: <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(q)=\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(q)=\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// Variant 1: Tiered Contrastive Reasoning</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
            Partition <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{H},P^{M},P^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{H},P^{M},P^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\text{tier}}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\text{Reflect}(P^{H},P^{M},P^{L}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>tier</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Reflect</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\text{tier}}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\text{Reflect}(P^{H},P^{M},P^{L}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// Variant 2: Multi-Metric Contrastive Reasoning</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each metric <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{m}\leftarrow\arg\max_{p_{i}\in\mathcal{R}(q)}\text{Score}(p_{i},m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{m}\leftarrow\arg\max_{p_{i}\in\mathcal{R}(q)}\text{Score}(p_{i},m)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
            <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{*}_{\text{metric}}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\text{Integrate}(P^{m},\forall m\in\mathcal{M}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext>metric</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Integrate</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\text{metric}}\leftarrow f_{\theta}(\text{Integrate}(P^{m},\forall m\in\mathcal{M}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">// Evaluation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
            Evaluate: <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Score}(\hat{y})=\mathcal{E}(p,p^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Score}(\hat{y})=\mathcal{E}(p,p^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct experiments on the <em id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">HelpSteer2</em> dataset to evaluate the effectiveness of our proposed Contrastive Reasoning Prompt Optimization (CRPO). All experiments are designed to ensure fairness in comparison with baseline methods by using the same retrieval pool and evaluation settings.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>1 </span>LLM and Retrieval Models</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For generations, we utilize two representative large language models:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4o</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>: accessed via API, configured with temperature <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure deterministic outputs. All other hyperparameters are kept at their default settings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLaMA 3-8B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>: an open-source instruction-tuned model, also set with temperature <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0</annotation></semantics></math> for reproducibility.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For retrieval, we adopt the BM25 retriever, which selects top-<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> reference prompts <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{1},\dots,p_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each query. We set <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=10</annotation></semantics></math> across all experiments, ensuring sufficient coverage across the <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation dimensions while maintaining efficiency.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
